{
  "seed": 1,
  "notes": "1908 three-storey mixed-use block, W side of Grant Avenue between Clay and Washington (831-843). Cream-painted brick with tall double-hung windows in dark brown sashes; the whole ground storey faced in polished dark green-black stone with narrow piers. Ground: four shopfronts (a grilled shop at the south end, an open-front shop, a display-window shop, a north shop) and a narrow glazed stair door between the first two. Two light steel fire escapes at second-storey level (wide south one with a hung drop ladder, narrow north one). Third storey: one long balcony with a light steel railing across most of the front; under its middle, a painted eave (yellow soffit, red and green rafters and brackets, green tile edge) over the second-storey windows. Plain parapet with a raised fret band; over the middle a small green-tiled crown roof. Flat roof. Signage: shop sign bands only (blank). Cream wall, brown sashes with curtains, polished dark-green veined stone ground storey, roll-down shutter on the south shop, painted skirt eave (yellow soffit, alternating red/green rafters, green tile rim), tiled crown with upturned corners over the parapet, raised key band, teal lattice panel in the balcony rail, grated fire-escape decks with a stowed drop stair, stocked shop windows, blank bordered sign boards, a projecting board, a window A/C unit and a downpipe. Gate fix (shutter on a kit material), dark raised key bands (left high under the parapet, right lower), shorter stowed drop ladder, softer crown upturns, warmer cream wall. The balcony eave is a shallow sloped soffit tucked under the 3rd-storey slab with strut brackets; a deeper hipped crown with finials over a bordered nameboard; one large key band either side of the crown; a folding scissor grille at the south shop; high-contrast sign boards with illegible procedural marks (no real sign text); darker stocked displays; longer drop ladder, a roof ladder, flagpoles, vents, curtains and heavier sashes. Weathered-ochre soffits; retail-density shop stock, garment rails, ceiling fixtures and a warm lining in the ground-floor shops. Yellow soffit back at about half depth, brick running bond in warm cream, see-through vertical-bar roll grille at the south shop, deeper sign fascias with a display plinth and transom, darker raised key bands, lower crown, grey steel fire escapes with the roof ladder at the north corner, dark brown sashes.",
